<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="Definitions_mixed_hot_cold" targetNamespace="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn">
  <!--
    Mixed hot/cold runtime-state workload.

    Most instances take the hot branch: one service task, completed by the load-test
    worker within milliseconds, so the instance's keys are deleted right behind the
    insert. The remainder take the cold branch and park forever on a 30-day timer and
    a message subscription that is never correlated, so their keys are written once
    and never touched again. The share of cold instances is set by the divisor in the
    condition below (4 => 25%); `businessKey` is the per-instance counter the load-test
    starter injects.

    Used to build a large body of cold state alongside a moving hot tail, which is
    what RocksDB's compaction file picker needs in order to behave differently
    between compaction_pri settings (see issue #56519).

    The cold branch writes a ballast variable before parking, so that settled state
    grows fast enough to reach the multi-GB regime (where RocksDB's base level
    reaches 1 and the bottom level is properly populated) within a run of ~13h.
    Without it, growth is ~650 bytes per parked instance, which needs ~150h.

    The ballast is a list of UUIDs. Entropy matters: the two deepest levels are
    LZ4-compressed, so low-entropy filler would inflate the logical state without
    growing the levels on disk. LZ4 manages only 1.05x on UUIDs, so the levels grow
    by what is written. It sits on the cold branch only — inflating the hot path
    instead would change the throughput the engine can sustain, and the moving hot
    tail is half the point of this workload.

    Size it by the element count below: each element costs 38 bytes, so 480 elements
    writes ~18.2KB per parked instance. Settled state grows by less than that: 300
    elements measured 7.46KB net per parked instance, not 11.4KB, because compaction
    reclaims the hot branch's tombstones against it. That measurement (0.252GB/h per
    partition at 110 PI/s, 3 partitions, R^2 0.9993 over a settled 40min window) is
    what sets 480: it puts growth near 0.47GB/h per partition, crossing the 3.2GB
    base-level-1 boundary around 7h so that a 13h run spends about half its length in
    the regime this workload exists to probe. 300 elements would cross it at 12.7h,
    i.e. in the final twenty minutes, which is no use.

    Do not re-derive the element count from first principles. Predicting it that way
    overshot the real slope by 51%; re-measure it on a settled DB instead.

    Costs, both measured: ~1.3ms of processing thread per parked instance at 480
    elements, and on disk ~0.47GB/h per partition of SST plus a roughly fixed journal,
    with snapshots nearly free because RocksDB checkpoints hard-link SST files (25-42MB
    of snapshot against 437MB of runtime). A 13h run lands near 40GB of a 64Gi volume.
  -->
  <bpmn:process id="mixedHotCold" name="Mixed hot and cold state" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:startEvent id="start" name="start">
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_start_split</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_start_split" sourceRef="start" targetRef="split" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="split" name="cold?" default="flow_split_hot">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_start_split</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_split_cold</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_split_hot</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_split_hot" sourceRef="split" targetRef="hotTask" />
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="hotTask" name="hot task">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:taskDefinition type="benchmark-task" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_split_hot</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_hotTask_hotEnd</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_hotTask_hotEnd" sourceRef="hotTask" targetRef="hotEnd" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="hotEnd" name="hot end">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_hotTask_hotEnd</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_split_cold" sourceRef="split" targetRef="coldBallast">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=modulo(businessKey, 4) = 0</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:scriptTask id="coldBallast" name="write ballast">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:script expression="=for i in 1..480 return uuid()" resultVariable="ballast" />
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_split_cold</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_coldBallast_coldFork</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:scriptTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_coldBallast_coldFork" sourceRef="coldBallast" targetRef="coldFork" />
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="coldFork" name="park">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_coldBallast_coldFork</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_coldFork_coldTimer</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_coldFork_coldMessage</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_coldFork_coldTimer" sourceRef="coldFork" targetRef="coldTimer" />
    <bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent id="coldTimer" name="30 days">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_coldFork_coldTimer</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_coldTimer_coldJoin</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:timerEventDefinition id="TimerEventDefinition_cold">
        <bpmn:timeDuration xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">P30D</bpmn:timeDuration>
      </bpmn:timerEventDefinition>
    </bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_coldFork_coldMessage" sourceRef="coldFork" targetRef="coldMessage" />
    <bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent id="coldMessage" name="never correlated">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_coldFork_coldMessage</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_coldMessage_coldJoin</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:messageEventDefinition id="MessageEventDefinition_cold" messageRef="Message_cold" />
    </bpmn:intermediateCatchEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_coldTimer_coldJoin" sourceRef="coldTimer" targetRef="coldJoin" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_coldMessage_coldJoin" sourceRef="coldMessage" targetRef="coldJoin" />
    <bpmn:parallelGateway id="coldJoin">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_coldTimer_coldJoin</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_coldMessage_coldJoin</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>flow_coldJoin_coldEnd</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:parallelGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="flow_coldJoin_coldEnd" sourceRef="coldJoin" targetRef="coldEnd" />
    <bpmn:endEvent id="coldEnd" name="cold end">
      <bpmn:incoming>flow_coldJoin_coldEnd</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmn:message id="Message_cold" name="cold-correlation">
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <zeebe:subscription correlationKey="=businessKey" />
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
  </bpmn:message>
</bpmn:definitions>
